      "id": 1,
      "text": "Selden, once known as Westfield, changed its name in 1852 to honor Judge Henry R. after postal conflicts forced a new identity.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.longislandguide.com/visit/selden/",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In the 19th century, Selden grew as a Suffolk County farm community, producing melons and early garden vegetables and housing a Presbyterian church built in 1857.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Selden,_New_York",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Between 1919 and 1959, Telescope Hill in Selden housed a fire‑lookout tower, and a German U‑boat was spotted from its peak during WWII.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Selden%2C_New_York",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Before European settlement, Selden’s land was part of the Setalcott tribe’s Algonquian‑speaking territory across northern Brookhaven.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
